A||||3||fiero56||finally dropped a PFF card in a Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||fiero56||06-09-2000||04:43 PM||||With today the last day of school for the summer, and probably my last day at this college, I was able to make time to stop by a red Formula I see parked near the sky-walk I use.<P>Very nice. It had a plain roof, was a 5-speed, and eq radio. It had an FOCOA sticker on the rear glass! I "made" a PFF card(wrote the address on notebook paper) and dropped it inside the car.<P>The Formula did have a few cool changes done to it.||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||06-09-2000||10:24 PM||||Cool..what kind of changes?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||06-10-2000||12:11 AM||||The owner took out lower portion of the decklid vent grills. Just the top half is there, looks very cool.<P>It also had a very well fitting bra on the front. Didn't notice if it said "Fiero" or not though.<P>The wheels also didn't look like the stock color.  If they were stock, they are in excellent condion, and must have had a little reflection coming off the car next to it.<P>There was also a rear mounted antenna. I didn't take the time to look everything over, but it was mounted in the rear somehow.||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||06-10-2000||09:52 AM||||next best thing besides dropping a card on a Fiero is carry a disposable camera with you.  I always carry one with me to take quick snap shots of Fieros!  <BR>Sometimes I even take shots of Fieros in junkyards!  I've learned you can never take an obsession too far!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
